  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 332 AM EDT Sun Aug 16 2026\n\nHeat will continue to be the big concern through the long term \nforecast. The models are in pretty good agreement that we will be at \nor just below heat advisory through the work week. Daytime highs in \nthe mid to upper 90s will yield apparent temperatures between 100-\n105 for all but the highest elevations of NE Georgia. \n\nThe pattern should break towards the end of the week as we return to \nmore NW flow and get a wave of precip on Friday and into Saturday. \nBeyond that, its difficult to say whether we clear out or if a \nstationary front sets up across the SE brining unsettled weather \nthrough the weekend and into next week. For now though, the main \nconcern will continue to be heat and afternoon thunderstorms; the \ndeep south in the summer.",
